  (section
    (heading "Implementation Notes")
    (subsection
      (heading "Critical Requirements")
      (item "1. **Real UDP Communication:** All tests use actual UDP sockets (no mocks)")
      (item "2. **Wire Format Compatibility:** Byte-identical packets across languages")
      (item "3. **Cross-Language Validation:** Python ↔ Swift must interoperate perfectly")
      (item "4. **No Assumptions:** Wire format match ≠ network interoperability"))
    (subsection
      (heading "SDTS Issue #1: AES-GCM Wire Format")
      (para "**Critical:** Swift CryptoKit and Python cryptography library MUST produce identical wire format:")
      (code "[nonce(12)] + [ciphertext] + [tag(16)]")
      (para "This is verified by Proto1 encrypted tests across languages."))
    (subsection
      (heading "Test Pattern")
      (para "**Sender (simple, synchronous):**")
      (code "let packet = build_packet(...)
send_udp(packet)
exit(0)")
      (para "**Receiver (full async stack):**")
      (code "receive_udp()
verify_hmac()
process_protocol()
exit(0 if success else 1)")
      (para "This pattern enables clean, isolated tests."))
    (subsection
      (heading "Debugging Failed Tests")
      (para "If tests fail:")
      (item "1. Check `/tmp/sender.log` and `/tmp/receiver.log`")
      (item "2. Verify test port is available (49999)")
      (item "3. Check firewall settings")
      (item "4. Run individual test manually to debug")
      (item "5. Verify Python and Swift implementations both completed Steps 1-14"))
    (subsection
      (heading "Adding More Languages")
      (para "When adding new language (e.g., Rust):")
      (item "Add sender/receiver programs in `tests/interop/rust/`")
      (item "Update master runner to include new combinations")
      (item "Total tests becomes N² × 12 (e.g., 3 languages = 9 × 12 = 108 tests)")))
